{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsKnots.mobius_frobenius_kernel","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.mobius_frobenius_kernel","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Normed.Group.Basic"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.nonempty_mobiusFrobeniusKernelContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.nonempty_mobiusFrobeniusKernelContext","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/mobius_frobenius_kernel.lean#L157-L161","doc":"**So `MobiusFrobeniusKernelContext` is inhabitable**, stated rather than\nleft to inference from the `def` above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.inverseSquareContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.inverseSquareContext","kind":"def","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/mobius_frobenius_kernel.lean#L143-L155","doc":"**A context exists.** The degenerate one: a `q`-independent kernel already\nequal to the inverse square, on `E = ℝ` with `γ = id`.\n\nDeliberately trivial. It witnesses that the three fields are **mutually\nconsistent** — which is all inhabitation can show — and it is emphatically\nnot the Frobenius–Hopf kernel, whose `q`-dependence is the entire content\nof reduction 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.mobius_frobenius_kernel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.mobius_frobenius_kernel","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/mobius_frobenius_kernel.lean#L108-L131","doc":"**Classical limit of the Frobenius–Hopf kernel is the repulsive\n`1/r²`** ([`lem:mobius-energy-frobenius-kernel`]) — the resolving\ndeclaration for `lean.ref`\n`qou:QOU.BraidsKnots.mobius_frobenius_kernel`.\n\nAt distinct filament points `γ(s) ≠ γ(t)`, the Frobenius–Hopf\nkernel `tr(Δ(γ(s)) ⊗ Δ(γ(t)))` collapses, in the deformation\nlimit `q → 1`, to the Möbius-energy kernel `1/‖γ(s) − γ(t)‖²`.\n\n**The statement is unchanged; the proof is now a derivation.** The body\nrewrites the target through reduction 2 and discharges it with reduction 1.\nPreviously it was `ctx.classical_limit s t hst` — a projection of a field\nthat *was* this conclusion. Both the old and the new version are sorry-free\nand report the same axioms, which is the point: `#print axioms` cannot tell\na derivation from a restatement, and did not. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:lem:mobius-energy-frobenius-kernel","label":"lem:mobius-energy-frobenius-kernel","md":"quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/mobius-energy-frobenius-kernel.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.MobiusFrobeniusKernelContext.killing_eq_inverse_square","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.MobiusFrobeniusKernelContext.killing_eq_inverse_square","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/mobius_frobenius_kernel.lean#L105-L105","doc":"**Reduction 2 — the Frobenius pairing reduces to the `SU(2)` Killing\nform, which evaluates to the inverse square.** Not the conclusion: a\npointwise identity between two kernels, containing no limit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.MobiusFrobeniusKernelContext.kernel_tendsto_killing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.MobiusFrobeniusKernelContext.kernel_tendsto_killing","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/mobius_frobenius_kernel.lean#L98-L98","doc":"**Reduction 1 — the `q`-Hodge star reduces to the classical Hodge star.**\nThe deformation limit exists and is the classical kernel. Not the\nconclusion: the limit point is `killingKernel`, an opaque field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.MobiusFrobeniusKernelContext.killingKernel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.MobiusFrobeniusKernelContext.killingKernel","kind":"def","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/mobius_frobenius_kernel.lean#L94-L94","doc":"The Frobenius pairing's **classical** (`q = 1`) kernel, carried\nabstractly. Kept separate from `1/r²` on purpose: the two fields below\nare then independent claims rather than one claim and its restatement. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.MobiusFrobeniusKernelContext.K_FH","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.MobiusFrobeniusKernelContext.K_FH","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/mobius_frobenius_kernel.lean#L90-L90","doc":"`q`-parametrised Frobenius–Hopf kernel: `K_FH q s t` is the trace\n`tr(Δ(γ(s)) ⊗ Δ(γ(t)))` of the Frobenius pairing at deformation\nparameter `q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.MobiusFrobeniusKernelContext.γ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.MobiusFrobeniusKernelContext.γ","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/mobius_frobenius_kernel.lean#L86-L86","doc":"Knot filament curve `γ : ℝ → E` (arc-length parametrised). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.MobiusFrobeniusKernelContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.MobiusFrobeniusKernelContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/mobius_frobenius_kernel.lean#L84-L84","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.MobiusFrobeniusKernelContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.MobiusFrobeniusKernelContext","kind":"class","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/mobius_frobenius_kernel.lean#L46-L106","doc":"Data of the Möbius-energy / Frobenius–Hopf-kernel claim\n([`lem:mobius-energy-frobenius-kernel`]).\n\n**RESTRUCTURED 2026-09-13 — the previous version carried the CONCLUSION\nas a field.** It had a single field `classical_limit` whose statement was,\nverbatim and with the same binders, the theorem below; the theorem's body\nwas `ctx.classical_limit s t hst`. That is the self-assuming projection\nAGENTS.md §3b-cond item 5 names, and the class docstring asserted the\nopposite of what the code did — *\"All fields are inputs; none is the\nconclusion\"* — while the conclusion was field three of three.\n\nThe two fields that replace it are **exactly the two reductions the\ntheorem's own docstring says the proof requires**, and neither is the\nconclusion:\n\n* `kernel_tendsto_killing` — the `q`-Hodge star reduces to the classical\n  Hodge star, so the `q → 1` limit **exists** and is the Frobenius\n  pairing's classical kernel. Its limit point is the abstract\n  `killingKernel`, not the target value.\n* `killing_eq_inverse_square` — the Frobenius pairing `∫_A ∘ μ` reduces to\n  the `SU(2)` Killing form, and that form evaluates to the inverse square.\n  A pointwise algebraic identity; no limit appears in it.\n\n**What this does and does not buy, stated plainly.** The *conjunction* of\nthe two is equivalent to the old single field — splitting an assumption\ndoes not discharge it, and this file still proves no analysis. What\nchanges is that the obligation is **localised**: an instantiator now faces\nthe two named unformalised reductions separately rather than one field\nspelling out the answer, and the theorem below **derives** its conclusion\ninstead of projecting it.\n\nThe second field is no longer an arbitrary target. `QOU.MobiusMutualChannel`\n§7–§8 prove the inverse square is the **unique** Möbius-invariant separation\nkernel — on unconstrained triples (`mobiusInvariant_forces_inverse_square`)\nand on geometrically realisable ones (`realisable_forces_inverse_square`),\nboth sorry-free. So `killing_eq_inverse_square` asserts that the Killing\nform lands on the kernel that symmetry independently forces, rather than on\na value chosen to match. ","signatureChunk":0}]}